{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"title","type":"text","x":0,"y":-260,"width":1920,"height":200,"text":"# DataManagement: ingestion and research run\n19–20 Nov 2026, Resource-Library, as it happened.\n🟩 done · 🟥 blocker · 🟧 fix (commit) · 🟦 decision · 🟨 open or middling · 🟪 output"},
		{"id":"i0","type":"text","x":0,"y":120,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"### 1. Move the research in\n20 outside-agent reports filed in Resource-Library as project **DataManagement research**, each marked *generated, unverified*. Nothing left in E:\\DataManagement.","color":"4"},
		{"id":"i1","type":"text","x":0,"y":410,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"### 2. Unblock folder decisions\nD:\\Librarian_V2 was stale (edited all day), so it blocked every decision in the library. Re-surveyed (119 s); 5 decisions re-applied, children first.","color":"4"},
		{"id":"i1s","type":"text","x":480,"y":410,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"**Fix `9c0592d`**\nAn excluded folder (`tmp`) no longer blocks accepts.\n*Still open:* every accept rebuilds every group (Geo-side, OP2).","color":"2"},
		{"id":"i2","type":"text","x":0,"y":700,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"### 3. Attach E:\\DataManagement\nFresh survey. `11` (needs OCR), `12` (books), `13` (retracted) and `_external` excluded by a person.","color":"5"},
		{"id":"i3","type":"text","x":0,"y":990,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"### 4. Clerk folder checks\nAll 23 failed with `FOLDER_DRAFT_FAILED`: no call reached a model.","color":"1"},
		{"id":"i3s","type":"text","x":480,"y":990,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"**Fix `cab623a`**\nQualification was lost between Cores: each wrote back its whole copy of the shared file. Saves now merge under a lock. All 5 Cores restarted and re-qualified.","color":"2"},
		{"id":"i4","type":"text","x":0,"y":1280,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"### 5. Folder checks and policy\nAll 23 subfolders came back normal; policy accepted them as research or third-party papers.","color":"4"},
		{"id":"i5","type":"text","x":0,"y":1570,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"### 6. Queue the papers\nA dry count found 0: each accepted subfolder is its own root. Queued per subfolder: **96 PDFs**, deferred, no model.","color":"4"},
		{"id":"i6","type":"text","x":0,"y":1860,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"### 7. Read them (batch)\nintake → approve → validate · parse · read · lenses · data · relate · metadata · review · publish\n**90 enriched, 6 partial**, under $1. Paper graph `…-DataManagement-third-party-papers` built.","color":"4"},
		{"id":"i7","type":"text","x":0,"y":2150,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"### 8. The missing last step\nNobody accepted them out of staging. The library held catalogue cards only; research found no papers to keep.","color":"1"},
		{"id":"i7s","type":"text","x":480,"y":2150,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"**Open point OP1**\nAn enriched-but-unaccepted backlog has no owner and no alert.","color":"3"},
		{"id":"i8","type":"text","x":0,"y":2440,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"### 9. Accept → Source notes\n90 accepted (agent promotion mode), 90/90 findable. 6 partials re-read and accepted. **96 Source notes**, named as in the graph, files still labelled `third_party`.","color":"4"},
		{"id":"g-ing","type":"group","x":-30,"y":60,"width":980,"height":2690,"label":"Ingestion: E:\\DataManagement → Source notes"},
		{"id":"r0","type":"text","x":1080,"y":120,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"### A. Frame the work\nProject note with standing disqualifiers; **Deeper research brief** with five questions (B1 query surface · B2 linking · B3 graph→context · B4 filing · B5 change impact).","color":"5"},
		{"id":"r1","type":"text","x":1080,"y":410,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"### B. Assign the Lead\nOwner's choice: **MiMo-V2.6-Flash**, recorded as an override.","color":"5"},
		{"id":"r2","type":"text","x":1080,"y":700,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"### C. Run 1\n`open_brief` asked a question nobody answered → thread parked. No phase offered `resume_session` → deadlock.","color":"1"},
		{"id":"r2s","type":"text","x":1560,"y":700,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"**Fix `7be7a44`**\nA person's message resumes a parked thread. Disqualifiers set on the project.","color":"2"},
		{"id":"r3","type":"text","x":1080,"y":990,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"### D. Run 2\nLooped on `macro_run('resume_session')` (no such macro), waiting 600 s each time. No Geo-Grapher tools in any bundle.","color":"1"},
		{"id":"r3s","type":"text","x":1560,"y":990,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"**Fix `0d6af41`**\nUnknown macro refused at once; research phases get read-only graph tools.","color":"2"},
		{"id":"r4","type":"text","x":1080,"y":1280,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"### E. Run 3: search, then judge\nReal graph reads. Search closed properly, but **82 candidates**, mostly our own design notes. Judge needed 82 decides at 1 unit each, with 12 units left.","color":"1"},
		{"id":"r4s","type":"text","x":1560,"y":1280,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"**Fix `ea6a30c`**\n`decide` takes a list. `source` and `reason` required: MiMo drops optional arguments (probed directly).","color":"2"},
		{"id":"r5","type":"text","x":1080,"y":1570,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"### F. Judge cleared, nothing kept\nAll 82 decided in ~6 calls. Synthesise refused: the papers were not notes, so not candidates, and no quote could cite them.","color":"1"},
		{"id":"r5s","type":"text","x":1560,"y":1570,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"**Owner's choice**\nBoth: ingest the papers as notes (step 9), and graph citations as evidence.\n**`1064cf0`**: `cite_as` can be a candidate and a claim source, checked against the paper's note.","color":"5"},
		{"id":"r6","type":"text","x":1080,"y":1860,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"### G. Run 4\nPapers put forward by `cite_as`, then Judge's budget ran out. The refusal said `request_budget`; no bundle offered it. Parked, honestly.","color":"1"},
		{"id":"r6s","type":"text","x":1560,"y":1860,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"**Fix `8129b3b`**\n`request_budget` in every phase. A person extended Judge +20, then Synthesise +50.","color":"2"},
		{"id":"r7","type":"text","x":1080,"y":2150,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"### H. Five reports drafted\nB1–B5 staged, **$0.44**. Middling: abstract-level quotes, one garbled claim passed, code places unread.","color":"3"},
		{"id":"r7s","type":"text","x":1560,"y":2150,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"**Fix `9fd2fe9`**\nPaper outline offered; Core tells the Lead its graph labels; Synthesise searches code; `unreadable` review verdict; review on.","color":"2"},
		{"id":"r8","type":"text","x":1080,"y":2440,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"### I. Redraft\nSection text read via the outline; code graph searched. **9 of 12 claims hold**, 3 unchecked (all full-PDF quotes). **$0.14**.","color":"4"},
		{"id":"r8s","type":"text","x":1560,"y":2440,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"**`81914de`** an unchecked review now says why.\n*Open:* one synthesis shared by five reports (OP3); review runs on the assigned Clerk, not `route_review` (OP8).","color":"3"},
		{"id":"r9","type":"text","x":1080,"y":2730,"width":440,"height":230,"text":"### J. Step back\nWorkflow map generated from the code + 8 use cases, 16 open points (**`f7f1510`**). Plan forward W1–W8 (**`57f1d37`**).","color":"6"},
		{"id":"g-res","type":"group","x":1050,"y":60,"width":980,"height":2980,"label":"Research: five-question brief → insight reports"}
	],
